  "summary": "The identified studies apply federated learning techniques, specifically described as 'decentralised training without pooled records', to the problem of predicting customer attrition. Results reported across these studies include an AUROC of 0.92 on the Atlas-ICU dataset [V0203], an accuracy of 0.78 on ChurnBench [V0201], and an F1 score of 0.64 on AgriSat-4 [V0204]. Another study reports an MAE of 0.85 on MetroFlow [V0202]. Additionally, a related study applying representation learning to customer attrition reported an MAE of 0.9 on Atlas-ICU [V0215].",
